#EXTINF:-1 group-title="ARTE Concert - Opera" tvg-id="1032655378" tvg-name="For years‚ The Magic Flute has been one of the most frequently performed operas at the Aix-en-Provence Festival. After an eight-year absence‚ Mozart’s work is now back in a production by Clément Cogitore. The French artist interprets the plot as a modern coming-of-age story: Tamino and Pamina leave the world of childhood behind and enter a reality in which beauty is fragile and truth uncertain.<br/>From 31.07.2026 05:00" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",Mozart: The Magic Flute - Festival Aix-en-Provence 2026 (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (31.07.2026)
