#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Culture - Arts" tvg-id="595556453" tvg-name="Gaming isn't all fun and games; there's an ideology and a world view behind each game. Trinity notes‚ as she plays her favourite games with political scientist Oliver Mauco‚ how often the protagonists are white men defending America from a foreign enemy. They then move on to Gal*Gun‚ and discuss the model of submissive femininity that it portrays. What if gaming was politics?<br/>From 20.02.2018 13:17" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",Art of Gaming - Ideology (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (20.02.2018)
https://arteptweb-a.akamaihd.net/am/ptweb/072000/072400/072478-004-B_SQ_0_VO-STE%5BANG%5D_03008292_MP4-2200_AMM-PTWEB_kMbTSpY23.mp4
#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Culture - Arts" tvg-id="1926724674" tvg-name="In literature and cinema‚ it is often the bad guys who captivate us the most. In video games‚ you can actually become them: the iconic Dark Vader (Star Wars: the Force Unleashed)‚ a violent psychopath (Man Hunt)‚ or even an immigration officer (Paper Please). Trinity and Yann Leroux plunge into the dark side of video games.<br/>From 21.11.2016 15:19" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",Art of Gaming - Bad Guys (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (21.11.2016)
